sequenceDiagram
    participant C as client (wlr-randr, kanshi)
    participant UI as compositor UI (wire_output_management, output_management, compositor_impl)
    participant RT as render thread
    participant K as kernel (KMS)
    participant W as worker

    C->>UI: create_configuration(serial); enable_head / disable_head; set_mode … set_adaptive_sync
    UI->>UI: every protocol error checked at its request (already_configured_head, already_set, invalid_*)
    C->>UI: apply (or test)
    alt used already
        UI-->>C: protocol error already_used
    else serial not current (a hotplug since its done)
        UI-->>C: cancelled
    else a head left out
        UI-->>C: protocol error unconfigured_head
    else
        UI->>UI: queued (one job at a time, four waiting)
    end
    UI->>UI: resolve → target (every head disabled, custom mode > 16384, scale > 10, VRR without vrr_capable, more heads than CRTCs → failed)
    alt the target is the current state (kanshi at login)
        UI-->>C: succeeded (nothing done)
    else a KMS change (mode, enable, disable, VRR)
        UI->>RT: config_test (staged targets at new modes, CRTC allocation for new outputs)
        RT->>K: TEST_ONLY | ALLOW_MODESET of every changed pipeline
        RT-->>UI: on_config_tested(ok)
    end
    alt test, or refused
        UI-->>C: succeeded / failed (nothing on screen changed)
    else apply
        UI->>UI: switch: enables, modes, VRR, transform, scale, position, disables
        UI->>RT: output ops with a ticket (add, switch_mode, set_vrr, retire)
        UI->>C: wl_output / xdg-output / heads events, done(new serial)
        RT->>K: one combined modeset carrying each changed output's first frame
        RT-->>UI: on_modeset_result(slot, ticket, ok)
        alt every changed output committed
            UI-->>C: succeeded
            UI->>W: 2 s later: outputs.toml (write, fsync, rename)
        else a modeset refused
            UI->>UI: switch back to the previous state
            UI-->>C: failed
        end
    end
